            "no --mount-proc: the setup script mounts a fresh /proc itself inside the PID namespace, so the flag set is `unshare -rnmpf --kill-child`",
            "pivot_root into a tmpfs root (old root detached) with a chroot fallback where pivot_root is refused, both with CAP_SYS_ADMIN and CAP_SYS_CHROOT dropped from the bounding set and no_new_privs set, so a root-in-userns command cannot mount or chroot out",
            "the command is the PID namespace's init (`exec`, not a wrapper): `$$` is 1, its exit status and signal death come back unchanged, and the namespace dies with it; the registered pid is the outer unshare",
            "/etc is a short list of copies (ld.so.cache, passwd, group, nsswitch.conf, hosts, localtime, \u2026), not a bind of /etc; python's /etc/python3* is deliberately left out so Debian's sitecustomize (apport, apt) does not run in the cage",
            "the mount point for the cage's root is an empty `<state>/sandbox/<sid>/root/` made at Sandbox.create, beside the home, so nothing is mounted over a host path and prune removes it with the home",
            "detection runs the whole cage first, then each half alone, so a machine that can only make some of the namespaces keeps what works (network off, or filesystem confined) and reports the rest",
            "four existing tests that relied on the shell reaching the state directory or the repository's tests/ were rewritten to the confined reality (AbortWhenSeen; the double crafter copied into the home)"
